**Issue**: #372
**Date**: 2026-09-07
**Status**: Approved
**Author**: NMG
**Related Spec**: specs/369-detect-execute-remediation-loops-and-close-workers-on-cancel/

Feature: Bare execute recovers the current incomplete delivery without looping
  Bare execute previously selected issues instead of resuming the current branch.
  One durable recovery allowance restores exhausted work without repeated attempts.

  @SCN001 @regression
  Scenario: Bare execute resumes the current branch's incomplete run
    Given the current branch has one exact matching incomplete execute checkpoint
    When the user invokes execute with no parameters
    Then its persisted queue and stage resume without a picker or recovery flags
    And only demonstrably stale ownership is recovered automatically
    And work, prior evidence and completed stages are preserved

  @SCN002 @regression
  Scenario: Exhausted recovery is durable and cannot become a loop
    Given a legacy run stopped after 13 implementation attempts
    When bare execute first recovers its exhausted stage
    Then exactly one durable recovery allowance is consumed before at most one worker dispatch
    And concurrent or repeated bare commands cannot create another allowance
    And later commits, summaries, failures or plugin upgrades do not reset that allowance

  @SCN003 @regression
  Scenario: Failed or ambiguous recovery remains stopped
    Given the recovery allowance for the current run issue and stage is consumed
    When the worker fails or dispatch or invocation loss makes its outcome ambiguous
    Then no automatic follow-on remediation or replay occurs
    And ownership and failed evidence remain durable
    And output reports the blocker without recommending another unchanged retry

  @SCN004 @regression
  Scenario: Validated recovery continues through delivery
    Given a resumed worker produces a genuinely validated passed handoff
    When execute advances the stage
    Then all remaining normal review verification and exact-head delivery gates continue
    And later stages retain their normal bounded remediation policy
    And an existing valid passed handoff needs no new repair dispatch

  @SCN005 @regression
  Scenario: Branch intervention and ownership stay fail-closed
    Given checkpoint, intervention or ownership evidence prevents safe recovery
    When bare execute is invoked
    Then no unsafe adoption intervention downgrade or duplicate worker occurs
    And only positively confirmed absent recorded panes are reconciled

  @SCN006 @regression
  Scenario: Discovery fallback and operator diagnostics remain complete
    Given no incomplete run or conflicting unreadable checkpoint exists
    When bare execute is invoked
    Then the existing specified-issue selection remains available
    And completed runs are not reopened
    And recovery status distinguishes available consumed and blocked work with actionable output
    And an isolated actual command and fresh registered smoke delivery prove the path
